{
 "_doc": [
  "BT1_R2: the soldier -> model table.  ONE row per unit key (every key of unitdefs.json `order` + the foe's e_* kinds).  Nothing here is code: to give a unit a real model, edit its row, nothing else.",
  "model   asset key of web/assets/<model>.glb (null = keep today's body).  The owner's number from a sheet decides which model; no row is filled without it.",
  "anims   asset key whose clips drive the model (null = the model's own clips; e.g. 'anims' / 'anims_army' for a model on the Quaternius UAL rig: bone names must match).",
  "h       the model's standing height in metres (the loader measures the file and scales it to this; null = the recipe's own scale).  yaw = facing offset in DEGREES (0 = the model looks to +z, 180 = to -z).",
  "clips   {idle, run, walk, atk, hit} clip names (string or list for a random pick); null = the recipe's own clip names.  ref = ground speed (m/s) at which the run clip's feet do not slide at scale 1 (null = recipe).",
  "lod2    {cloth, legs, skin, h} hex colours of the far-away figure (null = the generic one).  Fallback for any failure (missing file, bad clip, no rig) = today's body, with a console warning."
 ],
